  "body": "<h2>In the Rhythm of Mountain Meadows and Shepherd Huts</h2><p>Podhale is a region where tradition is still alive and the mountains set the rhythm of the day. Here, among high peaks and green valleys, one can feel true freedom and ease.</p><p>A walk along Krupówki can be overwhelming, but just stepping into one of the side streets reveals wooden architecture that delights with its simplicity and authenticity. Here, in the shade of old houses, you can feel the spirit of the old Podhale.</p><h2>The Art of Mountain Relaxation</h2><p>Slow travel in Podhale is above all about escaping toward nature. It is a hike through Strążyska Valley, where the murmur of the stream and the scent of dwarf pine let you forget the city noise. These are moments when time ceases to matter and the only goal is to reach a place where you can sit and simply look at the mountains.</p><p>An evening by the campfire with traditional oscypek cheese and the sounds of highland music is a ritual that lets you reconnect with tradition and people. Here, in an atmosphere of community and joy, one can find peace and energy for further life.</p>",
